From fda9a8ad6aa1f9795252acf29cc0765e07fbdef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheCryptoDonkey <TheCryptoDonkey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:49:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: read an encrypted store whose nonce starts like JSON

A sealed store file starts with its random nonce, which is { or [ in 2 of
every 256 saves. The message store and mesh contacts checked that first
byte alone, read such a file as plaintext, failed to parse it and loaded
an empty store, which the next save wrote over the file.

storage_crypto::open_stored tries the key first and accepts plaintext only
if it also parses as JSON. The on-disk format is unchanged.
---
 core/archipelago/src/mesh/mod.rs       | 28 +++-----
 core/archipelago/src/node_message.rs   | 26 +++----
 core/archipelago/src/storage_crypto.rs | 97 +++++++++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)

